<article class="space-y-8 text-gray-700 leading-8">
    <header class="space-y-4">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary">
            OnnaSoft · Business technology
        </p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold leading-tight text-gray-900 md:text-5xl">
            Terms of Service: Clear Conditions for a Trusted Relationship
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-gray-500">
            At OnnaSoft, we believe that successful technology partnerships
            begin with transparency, trust, and clearly defined expectations.
            These Terms of Service explain the general conditions governing
            access to our website, interactions with our team, and the use of
            our technology services and solutions.
        </p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">
            Acceptance of These Terms
        </h2>
        <p>
            By accessing our website or engaging with OnnaSoft services, you
            agree to comply with these Terms of Service and any additional
            conditions communicated to you for specific products, projects, or
            agreements. If you do not agree with these terms, you should
            discontinue using the relevant services or website features.
        </p>
        <p>
            These terms are intended to establish a clear understanding of the
            responsibilities and expectations between OnnaSoft and its users,
            clients, and business partners. Specific projects may be governed by
            separate proposals, statements of work, service agreements, or
            contracts that define additional requirements.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">
            Our Technology Services
        </h2>
        <p>
            OnnaSoft provides technology services that may include custom
            software development, business process automation, Odoo
            implementation and customization, IT consulting, IT outsourcing, API
            integration, data science, big data solutions, and cloud migration.
        </p>
        <p>
            The scope, deliverables, timelines, technical requirements, and
            pricing of each engagement will be defined in the applicable
            proposal or service agreement. We work collaboratively with clients
            to understand their objectives and deliver solutions aligned with
            their business needs.
        </p>
        <p>
            Service availability and implementation timelines may depend on
            project complexity, client requirements, access to systems,
            third-party services, and the timely provision of information or
            approvals.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">User Responsibilities</h2>
        <p>
            When using our website or services, you agree to provide accurate
            information, communicate requirements clearly, and use our platforms
            and resources for lawful purposes. You must not attempt to gain
            unauthorized access to systems, interfere with service operations,
            introduce malicious software, or engage in activities that could
            compromise security or availability.
        </p>
        <p>
            Clients are responsible for providing the information, credentials,
            permissions, content, and decisions reasonably necessary for their
            projects. They must also ensure that they have the appropriate
            rights and authorizations to provide any data, software, or
            materials supplied to OnnaSoft.
        </p>
        <p>
            Delays caused by incomplete information, unavailable resources,
            changes in requirements, or delayed approvals may affect project
            schedules and deliverables. Any resulting adjustments will be
            addressed according to the applicable agreement.
        </p>
    </section>

